60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Option A seems lovely. It uses local people and doesn't seem to put too much pressure on our tired conservation lab.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option D is a disaster waiting to happen. Partner collections mean shipping delays and high costs. I vote to eliminate it immediately.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Option B is intriguing because of the working bench! People love seeing the process. It's human, it's real, and it's exciting.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option C is out. Overhead rigging in the suspended bay is too risky given the weight limits and the failure rate of powered displays.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Sakura,,Option A and B sound the cheapest! No fancy shipping from far away means the budget monster won't wake up!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, a working bench in Option B sounds wonderful, but will it add more work for the one person in the lab?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Option A is the most logical. It minimizes logistics, avoids the suspended bay's risks, and keeps the budget under control.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, the bench is a display, not extra work! Option B is a winner because it's a live experience. That's what brings people back.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Option B is safer than C, but we must ensure the ""reconstructions"" aren't too heavy. However, A is the safest for the building.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Sakura,,I like the idea of the working bench in B! It's like a little mystery happening right in front of us!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I still feel Option A is the kindest choice. It celebrates our community and doesn't stress our limited staff.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"Option B is acceptable, but A is superior in terms of risk management. No loans, no rigging, no technical failures.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shion, you're choosing the ""safest"" path to a boring show. Option B has that spark of life that the visitor comments are begging for.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I can support B if the reconstructions are light, but A is the only one that guarantees no structural or technical issues.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"I'm torn! B is exciting, but A is definitely the one that won't have hidden costs. Let's go with the one that's fun and cheap!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,Let us decide. I believe the well-being of our staff and the joy of our local artisans make A the best choice.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,Logic dictates that we avoid the risks of B's reconstructions and D's shipping. A is the only flawless choice.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I'll fight for B until the end! It's the only one that actually treats the gallery as a living space rather than a warehouse.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I will vote for A. The building cannot take any more risks this season. Stability is the priority.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'll go with A! I want to see if we can actually save money for once and maybe buy some better snacks for the breakroom!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
